68: /**
69:  * "Create RFQ From PR" form.
70:  *
71:  * Flow:
72:  *  1. Choose RFQ Date, RFQ Topic and Requisition (all three on one line).
73:  *  2. Selecting a requisition opens a popup with its eligible lines.
74:  *  3. Tick lines in the popup and click "Add Line" -> they appear in the lines table
75:  *     (the table grows with the number of lines).
76:  *  4. Choose an RFQ Term -> its text is filled into Terms and Conditions.
77:  *  5. OK creates the RFQ.
78:  *
79:  * Rules (same as RequisitionRFQService):
80:  *  - Only requisition lines not used in any RFQ/PO
81:  *    (M_RequisitionLine.XX_RfQ_ID null, C_OrderLine_ID null)
82:  *  - C_RfQLine.XX_RequisitionLine_ID is set
83:  *  - After save, M_RequisitionLine.XX_RfQ_ID is set
84:  *    (void/delete releases it via RfQVoidEventHandler)
85:  *  - Organization is not on the form: login org is used, otherwise the requisition's org.
86:  *
87:  * RFQ Term source: the term column of C_RfQ (the one the RfQ window uses) is detected
88:  * automatically from the Application Dictionary, so the dropdown shows the same terms.
89:  */
